# EAS Build archives the whole git repository (this folder), not just mobile/, so its
# ignore file must live here. Only mobile/ is needed to build the app: everything else
# (backend code, its .env with server secrets, test audio) stays off Expo's servers.
/*
!/mobile

# Reinstalled / regenerated on the build server.
/mobile/node_modules
/mobile/android
/mobile/ios
/mobile/.expo
/mobile/dist
/mobile/web-build
/mobile/.idea

# Local builds and the release signing key — never upload.
/mobile/debug-builds
/mobile/release-builds
*.apk
*.aab
*.keystore
*.jks
*.p12
*.log

# mobile/.env is deliberately NOT ignored: its EXPO_PUBLIC_* values (API URL, Supabase
# URL + anon key) are public client config that must be baked into the build. Keep
# only EXPO_PUBLIC_* values in it.
